00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:03.270 align:start position:0%
 
well you're right  thor love and thunder is the funniest  marvel movie to ever hit the silver  screen but it was also able to find a  way to fix the character of thor within  all the screaming goats naked gods and  jealous weapons but before we get into  it here is your official spoiler warning  we will be revealing spoilers for all of  thor love and thunder so if you don't  want to spoil the movie this isn't the  video for you quite yet taika waititi's  work on this film was absolutely  hilarious  and you can see his mark on almost every  scene in the movie to truly understand  how love and thunder fixed thor though  we'll first need to dive into the  character arcs he's had throughout the  mcu catalog before talking about the  hilarity that is thor love and thunder  [Music]  throughout the mcu thor has gone through  what i see as two major character arcs  the first arc spanned across thor thor  the dark world and thor ragnarok while  the second included avengers infinity  war avengers end game and now thor love  and thunder the other two movies he  appeared in the avengers and avengers  age of ultron gave him very little  screen time and next to no character  development so i'm mostly gonna just  ignore them in his first character arc  thor went from being a spoiled god  thinking only of himself and glory in  battle to someone who had lost  everything but still striving to be the  hero that his people needs i see his  first arc as one where a spoiled kid  sees true loss for the first time in his  life and it doesn't stop with just one  tragedy he loses his powers his brother  his best friends his mother his brother  again his home and his girlfriend these  movies tell a story of loss and  heartbreak with just one disaster after  another thor begins his arc as being  unworthy of even wielding mjolnir and  ends his arc understanding the asgard is  a people not a place thor's second  character arc begins with a hero who  continues to face loss and fails to save  his people falls into a depressive  vengeful state and redeems himself in  the end as a wholesome comedic hero  korg's intro to love and thunder says it  best he went from dad bod to god bod but  then went back to being a dad this  second arc tells a story of a god trying  to find his place in the universe  finally succeeding in love and thunder  he feels immense guilt for his inability  to defeat thanos before he snapped half  the universe away starts to redeem  himself and end game and fully realizes  his potential as a hero in the ark's  third act the main difference between  thor's first arc and his second is that  the first tells the story of a tragedy  while the second tells the story of a  comedy understandably both arcs have  major tragic events such as the loss of  asgard and even jane foster's death but  the main difference lies in each arc's  ending a tragedy always ends with a  disaster or heartbreak while a comedy  ends with a reunion or joy the first arc  was a tragedy because it ended with the  complete destruction of asgard and thor  ragnarok the second arc was a comedy  though because it ended with thor taking  on the mantle of fatherhood with gore's  daughter love giving meaning to the  movie's title thor love and thunder it's  even more meaningful too when you  realize that thor's new daughter figure  is actually played by chris hemsworth's  daughter in real life india rose  hemsworth while both sets of movies have  both tragic and comedic events they're  truly separated by who thor is at the  end of each arc you might be wondering  though how exactly did love and thunder  fix thor and how was he broken in the  first place  after the events of avengers infinity  war and endgame we were left with a sad  fat defeated thor with a big lebowski  mentality and no idea what his place was  in the world love and thunder brought  some life back into the character of  thor and all of the comedy we saw in  ragnarok although it's pretty cheesy and  campy thor finds himself and his place  in the universe as a dad fighting  alongside his new love love he  experiences more heartbreak with the  death of jane foster but he's able to  get closure and move on from their  relationship something he had never been  able to do before when all he got was a  note from her this movie fixed thor and  gave us a hilarious wholesome rom-com  with tons of little details that i loved  the opening guitar riff during the  marvel studios intro sequence was just  perfect along with all of the music in  the film the cinematography and use of  color in the movie was also great which  is to be expected from taika waititi  known for his striking color usage and  vibrant films i love the 80s vibes  present throughout the movie and all the  little details that could be easy to  miss on the first watch this movie was  chock full of hysterical moments like  frigga carrying a baby thor onto the  battlefield or thor riding stormbreaker  off a mountaintop like a witch on a  broom it was great to see matt damon and  chris hemsworth's brother luke hemsworth  return to play the stage actors we saw  in ragnarok alongside melissa mccarthy  as hella i loved seeing thor's new  tattoos of his brother loki across his  back as well as thor having some of  loki's hair braided into his own thor's  giant screaming goats tooth nasher and  tooth grinder were great to see too and  the film had some hilarious one-liners  such as when gore tells thor to call  stormbreaker and thor says only if you  call a dentist one of my favorite things  though was how the weapons in the movie  are treated like characters thor talks  to mjolnir and stormbreaker almost like  he's dating them and stormbreaker gets  jealous when thor seems interested in  the newly put together mjolnir it's just  hilarious to see thor interact with the  weapons like this when we've hardly  thought of them as characters of their  own before some of the funniest scenes  happened near the end of the film though  when we got to see little asgardian kids  given the power of thor momentarily  using stuffed rabbits as weapons and  also a little detail of korg making a  baby with someone named dwayne perhaps  nicknamed dwayne the rock something the  mid credits scene also got me super  excited because it showed us hercules  played by brett goldstein aka roy kent  from apple tv pluses ted lasso i can't  wait to see this rageful actor punch his  way into the mcu and get revenge for his  dad zeus  anyways leaven thunder was hilarious and  it had taika waititi's influence  throughout all of it the biggest thing  this movie had going for it though was  that it gave one of the best romance  stories we've ever seen in the mcu  before jumped only by wanda and vision  story and it just so happened to take  place in a rom-com  it was a bit stunning to see such a  comedic movie too especially right on  the heels of what i'd call a horror  movie in doctor strange and the  multiverse of madness it'd be hard to  find two movies in the mcu that were  more different than these two and they  came out right after one another i don't  have too many negative things to say  about the movie other than pointing out  a couple of plot holes which could  probably be answered by thor just  forgetting they were an option the first  lies in thor being able to give other  people his powers like we saw him give  the asgardian children near the end of  the film if he could give other people  his powers why didn't he do so in the  battle against thanos also if thor was  able to reach infinity with stormbreaker  and have any wish granted why didn't he  think to make a visit and wish thanos  never got the infinity stones while  these may seem like pretty significant  plot holes i'm not too bothered by them  and still absolutely love the movie but  let me know what you think did love  thunder live up to the hype or did it  fall short from ragnarok drop your  thoughts in the comment section below  also check out the video on your screen  for some more of my content don't forget  to like and subscribe and thanks for  watching rocket riley  [Music]

